# The forest and the moat: Act 1, level 1
# DRAFT by Claude for Matt to mark up (2026-11-12), for N4. Built only from
# pieces that exist today, and the scorpion's hunt, the slash and the portal
# that merged after G2. Nothing is built from it until Matt approves it.
#
# What the forest is today (shot 2026-11-12): the left half is one ground
# floor under a canopy road, the right half one long hill with the nest on
# top, and about a third of its twenty screens have no beat in them. The
# wall teaches the sill, bats on ladders, the switch and the floor that holds
# once, so this level leaves those alone and teaches the verb itself.
#
# Kept: the oak with its vine and boughs, the river crossed in the branches,
# the island, the hollow log, the nest, the culvert under the wall. Cut: the
# flat run between the island and the hill, and the hill's long bare slopes.
# Sixteen beats, so the level gets shorter than today, not longer.
ideas: throw and catch on the move, a sword in wood is a ledge, the cracked branch, the scorpion's back
also: the portal, two beats here (see the foot)

## 1. The clearing  [breather]  floor 1
The forest edge at dawn. A brazier, a chest, nothing alive. Trees close in
on the right, so the first thing you see past the light is wood.
brazier: here

## 2. The sleeper  [introduce: throw and catch on the move]  floor 1
A scorpion asleep with its back to you, on open ground. Throw: it dies.
Walk on while the sword is out and it comes home to where you are now,
not to where you threw from. It only wakes if you walk up to it, so a
bad first throw costs nothing.
can kill you: the scorpion, once woken

## 3. The oak  [introduce: a sword in wood is a ledge]  floors 1 to 3
The great oak. The vine climbs its trunk to the second bough and stops.
The third bough is a body's height above, over bare bark. A sword in the
trunk is the step. A miss drops you to the second bough, not the ground.
note: the vine and five boughs are today's; only the vine is shortened.

## 4. Under the boughs  [introduce: the scorpion's back]  floor 1
Past the oak's roots, a scorpion awake on a short patrol under the lowest
bough. On the ground it sees you and hunts, armour first, and a level
throw bounces. From the bough above it cannot see you: wait for it to
pass under, drop in behind it, and throw into its back.
can kill you: the scorpion
note: depends on the hunt's sight (#203), "its own floor" being within 40 px.

## 5. The shallows  [introduce: the cracked branch]  floor 1
The river's edge. A cracked branch over shallow water with mud under it,
no spikes. Stand on it and it shakes and drops you a short way into the
mud. The rule is learned by being let off.

## 6. The river  [develop: the cracked branch]  floors 1 to 2
Branches over the spiked riverbed, sound and cracked mixed, no two gaps
alike. A bat circles over the far half. Throw at it from a branch and
keep going: the catch comes to the branch you are on now. Standing still
to watch the throw is how a cracked branch takes you.
can kill you: the bat, the riverbed
note: develops throw and catch on the move too.

## 7. The island  [introduce: the portal]  floors 1 to 4
Mid river, a door in a stump that opens for three seconds, shuts, then its
twin opens in the canopy above. Run in and you come out up there, still
running. Both ends are safe here. Going back down is the same door.
brazier: on the island
loop: the canopy door brings you back to this brazier

## 8. The hollow log  [combine: a sword in wood + the scorpion's back]  floor 2
A fallen trunk across the far bank, hollow, with a scorpion in it. In the
tunnel it is a sword fight, face to face. The answer is to climb over the
log first and put a sword in its far end, go round to the near end, and
recall: the sword comes home through its back.
can kill you: the scorpion

## 9. The canopy road  [develop: a sword in wood is a ledge]  floor 4
Treetops over the river, the gaps between crowns too wide to jump, a
trunk in each. A sword in the trunk is the midway step, and you recall it
from the far crown. The stake is the riverbed below.
can kill you: the riverbed, two bats

## 10. The crown  [pocket]  floor 5
Up the tallest tree, a fourth sword lying at the top. Reached by two
swords in the bare trunk as steps, so you climb with one in hand and
recall both from the top.
note: twists the ledge (the step you left is in your way home), Matt's call.

## 11. The hill's foot  [breather]  floor 1
The canopy comes down to the ground at the start of the hill. A brazier,
a chest, a view of the castle wall above the trees.
brazier: here

## 12. The terraces  [twist: the cracked branch]  floors 1 to 3
The hill's face is terraces with cracked branches as the only steps
between them. Until now you kept off them; here you must land on one and
jump again before it goes, three in a row, each a different gap. Throw at
the bat from the bottom terrace and climb: the catch finds you two
terraces up.
can kill you: one bat
note: also twists throw and catch (the catch is above you).

## 13. The nest  [twist: the scorpion's back]  floor 3
Three scorpions on the hilltop. Each one that sees you comes to the edge
of its floor and waits facing you, so walking up the hill never gives you
a back. The answer that worked (drop in behind) has no bough to drop from.
Go round.
can kill you: three scorpions
note: depends on the hunt's instant turn (#203). If a turn delay goes in,
this beat gets easier.

## 14. The branch over the nest  [combine: the cracked branch + the scorpion's back]  floors 3 to 4
Round is a cracked branch from the hill's last oak, out over the nest. It
drops you into the middle of the three, behind the one nearest. Throw
before the others turn, then recall through the second.
can kill you: two scorpions

## 15. The door down  [develop: the portal]  floors 3 to 1
Past the nest, a door that takes you down to the moat bank. It comes out
beside a bat's circuit, so arriving is a risk, and the door back up comes
out at the nest's edge, so returning is one too.
loop: the door back up to the brazier at 11

## 16. The moat bank  [combine: throw and catch on the move + the scorpion's back]  floor 1
The bank under the castle wall, a scorpion hunting along it and the culvert
mouth at the far end. A throw at its face bounces. Throw anyway, then
somersault over it: it turns to face you on the far side, and the sword on
its way home comes in through its back. The bat's circuit is above the
somersault, so the jump has to be timed. The culvert is the way out, one way.
can kill you: the scorpion, the bat

# The count
# Each idea and its four beats, for Matt to check at a glance.
# - throw and catch on the move: 2, 6, 12, 16
# - a sword in wood is a ledge: 3, 9, 10 (pocket), 8
# - the cracked branch: 5, 6, 12, 14
# - the scorpion's back: 4, 13, 8, 14 and 16 (develop is missing; 8 does
#   the job but is a combine)
# - the portal: 7, 15. Two beats, not four. Either give it a twist and a
#   combine (a door that opens on a hunting scorpion; a sword thrown into a
#   door) or keep it as the level's way round rather than one of its ideas.
# - loops: 7 (canopy door to the island), 15 (moat door to the hill).
#
# Questions for Matt
# 1. The portal: an idea with four beats, or the way round? (above)
# 2. Beat 8 asks you to plan two moves ahead. Too much for level 1?
# 3. Beat 16 needs a bounced throw to keep coming home, and a somersault
#    over a 34 px scorpion. Neither is proved yet; Claude benches it first.
# 4. A pocket on the low road too (the dragon's cage seen through the trees,
#    as LEVELS.md wants it visible from Act 1)?
